  "body": "## What changed\n\nSeven mill posts now lift Z and name the next setup before a setup-change M0 or M1: Haas, Mazak, Doosan DNM, Sinumerik, Heidenhain, grblHAL and TinyG.\nEach post sanitizes the setup name and clears the marker after its section.\nOrdinary operation stops keep their existing output.\nDoosan cancels active TCPM before its reference return.\nHeidenhain uses the section's work clearance and refuses missing or unsafe clearance by operation name.\nIts move preserves a higher current Z and does not promise a machine-home position.\n\nThe branch starts directly from upstream/main 62e1d36a, as requested.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe app already sends `SetupChange` beside `AfterOperation` at a setup boundary.\nThese posts ignored the setup marker and emitted an ordinary stop.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe `camcraft-post` suite `setup_change` has 14 passing pins.\nThe seven `*_setup_change_retracts_and_names_next` tests cover M0 and M1, comment order, Z-only motion, sanitized names, and marker reset.\n`ordinary_stops_do_not_add_setup_change_motion` pins unchanged ordinary stops.\n`unhomed_grblhal_and_tinyg_setup_changes_use_work_clearance` pins the existing unhomed retract path.\n`heidenhain_setup_change_refuses_missing_or_unsafe_clearance_by_name` pins missing and unsafe clearance refusals.\n`heidenhain_setup_change_never_lowers_a_tip_already_above_clearance` pins the higher-tip rule.\n`heidenhain_setup_change_does_not_reuse_previous_sections_stock_top` pins section-local validation.\n`doosan_setup_change_cancels_tcpm_before_reference_return` pins cancellation before G28.\n`sinumerik_setup_change_refuses_an_unstated_machine_retract` pins refusal before any guessed lift or invitation to change setup.\n\nThe regression pins failed against unchanged upstream posts.\nThe ordinary-stop compatibility pin passed before the fix.\n\nAll 21 mutations failed with the protection removed and passed after restoration:\n\n- Each of the seven posts restored from upstream/main.\n- Each of the seven posts with its setup-marker reset removed.\n- Heidenhain with each check for clearance, stock top, clearance above stock, per-section stock reset, and preservation of a higher tip removed.\n- Doosan with TCPM cancellation removed.\n- Sinumerik with the return when `safeZ()` is null removed.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed 553 tests: 273 post tests and 280 app tests.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed after correcting two test-only collapsible-if lints.\nThe final setup-change run passed all 14 pins.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nNo `.nc` or `.cl` golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo real controller or machine was exercised.\nLathe and wire setup-change handling remains unchanged, including its existing stops without a new setup-change notification.\nThe mill Z-lift contract does not apply to `fanuc-lathe.cps`, `tormach-lathe.cps`, or `wire-iso.cps`.\nLathe departures need their own axis ordering around the stock.\nThe wire post cuts the wire and declares no trusted home position.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #1821 touches Haas, Mazak, Doosan DNM and Sinumerik in `onCycle`.\nThis PR changes `afterOp`, `onParameter`, and setup-change state.\nIt touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nThis PR is not stacked.\n\nChangelog: Seven mill posts now retract Z and name the next setup before a setup-change stop; Heidenhain refuses a setup change without safe work clearance.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nFixes #1647\n",
